tor from a social considerations perspective.","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"}],"business":[{"body":"The company's aerospace and defence segments are expected to drive growth, with increasing demand for specialized metal castings and components.","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| — | — | — | — |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"},{"body":"- Aims to build 'Parity' — helping India stand at par with the world in capability, technology, and quality for aerospace and defence.\n- Platform-independent core manufacturing technologies serving the full aerospace & defence spectrum (civil aviation, space, land/naval defence, strategic systems).","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Rating Upgrade] ICRA upgraded PTCIL's long-term rating.\n- [Industry Recognition] Named in Financial Times and TIME with Statista lists, validating sustained growth.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"Operating income: Rs. 308.1 crore (FY2025), Rs. 377.3 crore (9M FY2026); PAT: Rs. 61.0 crore (FY2025), Rs. 41.6 crore (9M FY2026); Net debt: Rs. 179.3 crore (September 30, 2025); Credit rating: [ICRA]A(Stable)/[ICRA]A1","src":"concall","title":"Financial scorecard / credit view"},{"body":"The company's operating profit margin is expected to improve over the medium to long term, aided by healthy scaling up of operations and improvement in profitability.","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"The company expects to incur a capex of Rs. 500 crore between FY2026 and FY2028, to be funded partly through debt, and aims to maintain a healthy financial risk profile, with expectations of improvement in profitability over the medium to long term.","src":"concall","title":"Guidance / outlook"},{"body":"The company has a strong order book, with some key long-term contracts, which is expected to aid the scale-up of operations.","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"The company's expansion into advanced materials, titanium and superalloy remelting, and large aerospace-grade component manufacturing is expected to provide growth optionality.","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials","investor presentation (03-06-2026)","Walk-the-Talk commitments ledger","credit-rating action (ICRA 27-03-2026)"],"thesis":"PTC Industries Limited is expected to witness strong revenue growth over the medium term, driven by its increasing presence in high-entry-barrier aerospace and space propulsion applications, and aided by the successful commissioning of key assets under its expansion programme.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[{"category":"strategic_priority","horizon":"2023-2026","item":"Carbon-footprint roadmap: measure Scope 1 and 2 in 2023, define reduction plan in 2024, measure Scope 3 by 2025, and take a global leadership role in carbon reduction from 2026.","promised":"Scope 3 by 2025; leadership by 2026 milestone","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"strategic_priority","horizon":"next 3-4 years (~FY27)","item":"Foreign OEM/export business to move from domestic-heavy today to a balanced, roughly equal split with domestic over the next three to four years.","promised":"50/50 domestic vs export %","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"target","horizon":"in 5 years (~FY28)","item":"Aerospace and defence business to grow from 15-20% of revenue today to 70-80% of total revenue over the next five years.","promised":"70-80 %","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"target","horizon":"in 5 years (~FY28)","item":"Aerospace castings plus aerospace materials segment to rise to over 70% of total revenue in the next five years.","promised":"70 %","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"new plant ramp (ongoing)","item":"Adding 300 tonnes/year of titanium casting capacity at the new 50-acre facility, via a large titanium casting furnace with over 400 kg metric melt capacity.","promised":"300 tons/year","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"new plant ramp (ongoing)","item":"Adding 300 tonnes/year of superalloy casting capacity (via a vacuum induction moulding furnace up to 1000 kg), taking combined new aerospace casting capacity to 600 tonnes/year.","promised":"300 (600 combined) tons/year","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"ongoing build-out","item":"Capex for the aerospace materials (titanium/superalloy metal) plant of about INR 170-180 crore, of which roughly INR 65-80 crore already spent.","promised":"170-180 INR cr","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"ongoing build-out","item":"Capex for the aerospace castings part of about INR 150 crore, of which only INR 10-15 crore has been spent so far.","promised":"150 INR cr","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"ongoing build-out","item":"Electron beam cold hearth remelting/refining furnace with capacity in excess of 5000 tonnes/year to recycle scrap titanium into aerospace-grade material.","promised":"5000 tons/year","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"ongoing build-out","item":"Vacuum arc remelting (VAR) line for titanium ingots/billets with capacity of around 1500 tonnes/year.","promised":"1500 tons/year","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"ongoing build-out","item":"Vacuum induction melting (VIM) equipment for superalloy raw materials with annual capacity of around 600 tonnes, using a 1000 kg furnace for special/intricate alloys.","promised":"600 tons/year","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"target","horizon":"at full capacity","item":"Green titanium via cold hearth recycling to cut carbon emissions by over 130,000 tonnes annually at full 5000-tonne capacity (~26 tonnes CO2 saved per tonne of recycled titanium).","promised":"130000 tons CO2/year","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"target","horizon":"new facility","item":"New 50-acre facility to source almost 50% of its power from renewable sources (solar).","promised":"50 %","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"ongoing","item":"Setting up a separate plant to assemble, fabricate and weld complete M777 ultra-lightweight howitzer titanium structures, using equipment relocated from BAE's shut UK plant.","promised":"text","quarter":"Q1FY24"},{"category":"risk_flag","horizon":"ongoing","item":"Titanium sponge supply is a future risk as most sponge production is in ex-CIS/Russia/China/Japan and the Russia-Ukraine war has squeezed supply.","promised":"text","quarter":"Q1FY24"}],"open_total":15,"quarters_n":1,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":1.17,"fy":"FY21","mcap":775.0,"opm":24.6,"pe":176.1,"roe":3.1},{"de":1.17,"fy":"FY22","mcap":2626.0,"opm":27.0,"pe":205.2,"roe":7.9},{"de":0.66,"fy":"FY23","mcap":3133.0,"opm":30.1,"pe":121.4,"roe":11.9},{"de":0.28,"fy":"FY24","mcap":10685.0,"opm":33.5,"pe":253.2,"roe":9.3},{"de":0.04,"fy":"FY25","mcap":22340.0,"opm":35.5,"pe":366.2,"roe":6.0}],"wtt":{"credibility_grade":"N/A","expired_n":"0","guidance_hit_rate":"","guidance_n":"0","isin":"INE596F01018","open_commitments":"15","projects_ontime":"0","projects_slipped":"0","quarters_covered":"1","reconciled_n":"0","revisions_n":"0","risks_recurred":"0","sector":"Capital Goods","summary":"Building track record — 1Q logged, no reconciled verdicts yet.","symbol":"PTCIL","theme_consistency_pct":"","tone_latest":"High-confidence, vision-heavy founder narrative; management acknowledged the miss on suppressed sub-10% ROE, framing it as the cost of a capability-investment phase now pivoting to capacity monetisation.","updated":"2026-07-12"}},"meta":{"co":"PTC INDUSTRIES LIMITED","isin":"INE596F01018","s":"PTCIL","sector":"Capital Goods"},"s":"PTCIL"}